Zedzy wrote:
> I've gone over the documentation repeatedly, and searched around here
> on USENET...and cannot for the life of me figure out how to change the
> game options. Specifically the "compounds" which cannot be changed
> in-game.
>
> The guide mentions doing so using NETHACKOPTIONS environment variables,
> or a configuration file. It's quite clear on the language used to do
> so, but I cannot figure out ~where~ to enter the information. Any
> advice would be much appreciated.
>
> I'm running 3.4.3 on OS/X Lion, using the Terminal.

On OS X, Linux, and BSD, you create a file called ".nethackrc" in your
home directory.

The content looks something like this:

OPTION=autopickup,autoquiver,autodig,pushweapon
OPTION=pickup_types:$/!?="
OPTION=pickup_burden:u
OPTION=!sparkle,!null,!timed_delay

